          <h2>How We Chose These Treadmills</h2>
<p>
            Not tested hands-on; picked from listings, specs and owner reviews. We did not run on these
            machines. We read each Amazon listing through Amazon’s product API on 21 November 2026, checked
            the maker’s own product page where one exists, and compared both with what this site has
            already published about each brand. Every figure on the page traces back to one of those sources.
          </p>
          <p>
            A treadmill had to clear five bars to make the list. <strong>It had to be on Amazon US between
            $400 and $600 on the day we checked.</strong> <strong>It had to be a real treadmill</strong>: a
            console on uprights, handrails, a motor listed at 2.5 HP or more (or, for Schwinn, a maker with
            a long published motor warranty) and a belt at least 18 inches wide. That rules out walking
            pads, however many horsepower their titles claim. <strong>It had to come from a named brand</strong> with a storefront or support contact beyond a single listing, which removed dozens of near-identical
            unbranded machines. <strong>Its basic figures had to be stated</strong>: belt size, weight limit and
            speed range at minimum. And <strong>it had to do one job better than the others here</strong>, so
            that the list gives a real choice rather than five versions of the same machine.
          </p>
          <p>
            We also avoided repeating the picks on our neighbouring budget pages where we could. The
            Goplus, WELLFIT and <a href="/xterra-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>XTERRA</a> machines on our under-$500 page and the NordicTrack T Series 5
            and Horizon T101 on our under-$800 page are all sensible buys, but they are covered there,
            and this page is more useful if it shows you the alternatives in the $550 to $600 band. Our guide
            to <a href="/how-much-does-an-xterra-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">what XTERRA treadmills cost</a> lists every XTERRA model, from the Compact folders up.
          </p>
          <p>
            We gave the most weight to belt size and weight limit, because those decide comfort and how
            hard the machine is worked, and to the warranty, because that is what protects you after
            Amazon’s return window closes. We gave little weight to peak horsepower figures and decibel
            claims, which are the numbers budget listings inflate most, and none to star ratings.
          </p>
