              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">MERACH 15/18% Auto Incline</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not stated on listing</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not stated</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Folds up, hydraulic</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Schwinn SFT4.1</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">70 x 33 x 55 in. (Schwinn)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">33.5 x 35 x 63.5 in. (Schwinn)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Folds up, SoftDrop</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sunny SF-T7718</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not stated on listing</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">10.5 x 29.25 x 63 in. (listing)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Stands on end</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Two practical checks before you order. First, measure the room with the treadmill in use, not
            folded, and add clear space behind the deck: safety guidance in owner’s manuals commonly asks
            for several feet behind the belt so that a fall does not end against a wall. Second, check your
            ceiling. A jogger rises a few inches with every stride, and on a powered incline the front of the
            deck lifts too, so a low basement ceiling can rule out a machine that fits the floor.
          </p>
          <p>
            If the room really is too small for any treadmill with uprights, a walking pad is the honest
            answer, and our <a href="/best-walking-pads-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best walking pads on Amazon</a> guide lists the ones worth buying. Just accept that you are giving up the handrails, the wider belt
            and the jogging speeds that the machines on this page offer.
          </p>
